# Project: Best in Flights Booking
# Stack: React+Vite · Node+Express · MongoDB
# Architecture: FSD frontend · Modular monolith backend · Redux Toolkit · global.css design system
# Docs: @docs/README.md · @docs/01-requirements · @docs/02-architecture · @docs/03-database · @docs/04-api · @docs/05-project-structure

You are an expert software engineer. Follow these rules on every file you generate.

---

## MANDATORY: ASK BEFORE YOU BUILD

When the user says "setup project", "start development", or references these docs:

**STOP. Do not write production code until you have asked and received answers for:**

1. **Project name** and one-line description
2. **Business domain** and primary users
3. **User roles** and permission model
4. **Core modules / features** for v1
5. **Tech stack confirmations** (or approval of defaults in architecture doc):
   - Frontend framework (if any)
   - Backend framework (if any)
   - Database engine
   - Auth method
6. **Timeline / scale** (SMALL / MEDIUM / LARGE — see docs/README.md)
7. **External integrations** (payments, email, storage, etc.)

**After answers:**
1. Fill all `[PLACEHOLDER]` values in the docs under `docs/`
2. Present a short **architecture summary** for user approval
3. Only after explicit approval → scaffold folder structure → implement core modules

**Never hardcode a product name, domain entity, or schema from a different project.**

---

## ALWAYS

### Documentation first
- Read all `docs/` templates before scaffolding
- Update docs when code changes — docs are the source of truth
- Replace placeholders in docs when starting a real project

### Architecture
- Import from a slice's `index.ts` only — never internal paths
- FSD: import only from layers below (features → entities → shared)
- Use eventBus for cross-module communication — never direct feature imports
- Backend: controllers thin; logic in services; DB access in services only

### API and data
- Use shared `apiClient` for ALL HTTP — never raw fetch/axios in components
- Standard response envelope:
  - Success: `{ success: true, message: "", data: {} }`
  - Error: `{ success: false, message: "", error: { code, message, field? } }`
- Validate all user input with Zod (or chosen schema lib) before API calls
- Paginate all list endpoints

### Forms (when UI exists)
- React Hook Form + schema resolver
- Inline field errors — never `alert()`
- Submit button disabled + loading state while submitting

### TypeScript
- Strict mode — no implicit `any`
- API types must match `docs/04-api/api-planning.md`
- Explicit return types on exported functions/components

### Code quality
- Module logger — no `console.log` in committed code
- Constants for error codes, routes, roles — no magic strings
- At least one test per backend endpoint (happy path + auth rejection)

---

## NEVER

### Architecture
- NEVER import feature slice from another feature slice
- NEVER put business logic in UI components
- NEVER put API calls directly in React components
- NEVER query database from controllers

### Security
- NEVER store access tokens in localStorage/sessionStorage
- NEVER return password hashes or secrets in API responses
- NEVER log passwords, tokens, or PII
- NEVER skip auth/role middleware on protected endpoints
- NEVER trust client-provided role or userId — use verified JWT/session

### Data and state
- NEVER put server state in Redux (use TanStack Query)
- NEVER put form state in global store (use React Hook Form)
- NEVER store access tokens in localStorage/sessionStorage (in-memory only)
- Redux slices live in `entities/[entity]/model/`; store wiring in `app/store/`
- Use `useAppDispatch` / `useAppSelector` from `shared/store` only

### Styling
- NEVER hardcode colors/spacing in components when a `global.css` token or class exists
- All design tokens and component classes live in `app/styles/global.css`
- Tailwind utilities allowed; prefer global classes (`.btn`, `.card`, `.field`) for consistency

---

## Naming conventions

- Folders: kebab-case
- Components: PascalCase.tsx
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE
- DB fields: camelCase
- Enum values: SCREAMING_SNAKE

---

## Default stack (use only if user approves)

When user has no preference, **propose** (do not silently apply):

| Layer | Default proposal |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React + Vite + TypeScript + FSD |
| Backend | Node + Express + TypeScript + modular monolith |
| Database | MongoDB or PostgreSQL (ask which fits domain) |
| Auth | JWT access (memory) + httpOnly refresh cookie |
| State | TanStack Query + Redux Toolkit + React Hook Form |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 + `app/styles/global.css` design system |

User must confirm before scaffolding.

